1
00:03:15,789 --> 00:03:21,789
And no one sings me lullabies. And no one makes me close my eyes.

2
00:06:31,578 --> 00:06:37,578
Pink Floyd: Live at Pompeii is a music,
documentary film directed by Adrian Maben.

3
00:09:47,368 --> 00:09:53,368
British progressive rock band Pink Floyd perform at the ancient Roman
Amphitheater in the ruins of Pompeii, Italy in 1971.

4
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:09,157
Although the band perform a typical live set from the era,
there is no audience beyond the basic film crew.

5
00:16:18,947 --> 00:16:24,947
Self - Bass, Vocals, played by Roger Waters.

6
00:19:34,736 --> 00:19:40,736
Self - Guitar, Vocals, played by David Gilmour.

7
00:22:50,526 --> 00:22:56,526
Self - Keyboard, Backing Vocals, played by Richard Wright.

8
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:12,315
Self - Drums, played by Nick Mason.

9
00:29:22,105 --> 00:29:28,105
Pink Floyd: Live at Pompeii is a 1972 concert film directed by Adrian Maben with the English rock
band Pink Floyd performing at the ancient Roman amphitheatre in Pompeii, Italy.

10
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:43,894
The band performs a typical live set from the era, but there
is no audience beyond the basic film crew.

11
00:35:53,684 --> 00:35:59,684
The main footage in and around the amphitheatre was filmed over four days in October 1971, using the band's regular touring
equipment, including a mobile 8-track recorder from Paris (before being bumped up to 16-track in post-production).

12
00:39:09,473 --> 00:39:15,473
Additional footage filmed in a Paris television studio the following
December was added for the original 1972 release.

13
00:42:25,263 --> 00:42:31,263
The film was then re-released in 1974 with additional studio material of the band
working on The Dark Side of the Moon, and interviews at Abbey Road Studios.

14
00:45:41,052 --> 00:45:47,052
The film has subsequently been released on video numerous times, and in 2002, a director's cut was released on DVD, which combined
the original footage from 1971 with more contemporary shots of space and the area around Pompeii, assembled by Maben.

15
00:48:56,842 --> 00:49:02,842
In April 2025, a 4K restoration, Pink Floyd at Pompeii – MCMLXXII, was shown in cinemas by
Trafalgar Releasing and Sony Music Vision, and released on home media shortly after.

16
00:52:12,631 --> 00:52:18,631
This was followed by an album with the remixed songs and outtakes, which was
released on 2 May 2025 and topped the music charts in several countries.

17
00:55:28,421 --> 00:55:34,421
A number of bands have taken inspiration from the film in creating
their own videos, or filming concerts without an audience.

18
00:58:44,210 --> 00:58:50,210
The film explores themes of concert, rock 'n' roll,
concert film, progressive rock, pompeii.
